# internal dogfood workspace — never publish
.tide/
# runtime launch registry: this repo is itself a control-home, so tide writes
# its sid→terminal map here. Machine-local state with an absolute home path —
# it must never be committed, and never ride into the release bundle.
terminals.json

# the project registry — terminals.json's twin, and the ONLY tracked file tide
# wrote itself. Its whole content is `name | /absolute/path`, so one `tide adopt`
# or `tide roster add` run in this checkout would commit a personal home path.
# It was safe only by being empty, which is a state, not a defence. No template is
# lost: `tide init` writes a fresh header-only roster into a real control-home
# (init_home.py), and nothing in install.sh or the wheel reads this copy.
roster.md

# черновики — только на диске. Под docs/ они уезжали на Pages и отдавались
# по прямым адресам, поэтому лежат в корне и не трекаются.
/drafts/
docs/drafts/
